{"id": "EUVD-2026-86939", "enisaUuid": "04d8b168-d475-38ad-a865-5e30e2850fe9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: L2CAP: fix chan mode for LE_CONN_REQ + EXT_FLOWCTL pchan\n\nl2cap_new_connection() sets default value of channel mode to match the\nparent channel.  l2cap_le_connect_req() left this at the default, and\ncreated L2CAP_MODE_EXT_FLOWCTL channels if listening pchan has that\nmode.  This causes FLAG_DEFER_SETUP channels to reply to\nL2CAP_LE_CONN_REQ with L2CAP_ECRED_CONN_RSP, which is incorrect.\n\nIt can also result to stack OOB write (of l2cap_alloc_cid determined\nvalues) in l2cap_ecred_rsp_defer(), as l2cap_le_connect_req() does not\nlimit maximum number of deferred channels or check for duplicate ident.\n\nFix by setting chan->mode correctly in l2cap_le_connect_req().\n\nAlso check channel mode in l2cap_ecred_rsp_defer(), and do WARN_ON_ONCE\ninstead of OOB write to make it less brittle.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:35:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:00", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad0f44a3f1f688558ed876a0702bc2c82b0df689", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/564ae0e05e598aa895b9dbd18cb7d6eb64752869", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aab17938998b29e75c3324763411aef3e300fc67", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e1fc7cab95ad958e55d70a5dfaaea687c9c639f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1074bcc57f741223f9fa82ce6afe5c3d783e4d10", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d5a625cbc854d4c4f68e4b16fcf6e682d9a9ed1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6cb79e6499228cfdbd4b3301371ce74d01cd2f80", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ef05db5b08b176a551b4a6287372045998806b0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-q3c9-52vx-cgp8", "CVE-2026-98108"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09ef8b3e-e1d7-3d27-abf3-03fec14f3880", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "19ee617e-c4f0-3403-ae96-5d526a2343a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <6cb79e6499228cfdbd4b3301371ce74d01cd2f80"}, {"id": "226ad4dc-dfa5-3272-9624-1cf493dbe98c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <5d5a625cbc854d4c4f68e4b16fcf6e682d9a9ed1"}, {"id": "2c01d76a-d6ce-3aba-a5d6-36f2247e0d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <0e1fc7cab95ad958e55d70a5dfaaea687c9c639f"}, {"id": "36a9d491-afd5-3bcf-982d-36d8f74c37cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3748ca9e-f688-3e52-99cd-497827eb63fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "3b06aee4-63a2-31d7-9998-1f553df471d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "54edb154-3499-3c4f-933c-c07588922f14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <ad0f44a3f1f688558ed876a0702bc2c82b0df689"}, {"id": "710f04c4-8940-3d98-a02e-6e186228fa45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <1074bcc57f741223f9fa82ce6afe5c3d783e4d10"}, {"id": "88ff8878-67a8-3fc6-816a-bb39b69d3506", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "a241280b-f7a7-38c7-bf3f-b43e547e6a8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "b131303f-fcd3-3b79-b479-25155eaaf4c8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "15f02b91056253e8cdc592888f431da0731337b8 <564ae0e05e59